{
    "benchmark_id": 195,
    "prompt": "Write a function that takes a grid which is a 2D array of objects, a starting position object with x and y coordinates, a maximum number of nodes to plant, and an array of plant positions. Each grid object has properties x and y for coordinates, value which is a number, and state which is a string. The plant positions array contains objects with x, y, and value properties that specify where to plant nodes and what values to assign. The function should perform a depth-first search starting from the given position, visiting adjacent nodes recursively and updating each visited node's state property to the string visited. After completing the depth-first search, the function should plant new nodes by using the positions and values from the plant positions array for nodes that have a value of zero, repeating this planting process until the maximum number of nodes specified has been planted or all plant positions have been used. The function should use a recursive approach and rely only on standard language features without external libraries or modules.\n\n    Only return the code, don't include any other information,\n    such as a preamble or suffix.\n",
    "implementation_details": "Language: JavaScript. Use recursion for the depth-first search and use the provided plantPositions array in order when planting new nodes; no external libraries or modules.",
